# Assignment: Make Listenify Interactive

Extend the Listenify application built in class into a *menu-driven console application* using Scanner. Reuse your existing Song, Album and PlaylistPlayer classes.

Display this menu repeatedly until the user chooses to quit:

text
========= LISTENIFY =========
0. Quit
1. Play next song
2. Play previous song
3. Replay current song
4. Show playlist
5. Remove current song
6. Pause / Resume
7. Add song to an album
8. Create album
9. Show available albums

Enter your choice:


- *Create album:* accept an album name and artist.
- *Add song:* display available albums, ask the user to select one, then enter the song title and duration. Ask whether to add it to the playlist.
- *Player controls:* connect the menu options to your PlaylistPlayer methods.

Handle invalid input and empty-playlist operations with helpful messages.

*Demonstrate:* create two albums, add songs from both to one playlist, and use the player controls. Actual audio playback and saving data after exit are not required.

Submit your Java source using the class Git branch and pull-request workflow.